# UNITARES Governance MCP - Environment Configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in your values:
#   cp .env.example .env

# ===========================================
# DOCKER CREDENTIALS (used by docker-compose.yml)
# ===========================================
# These default the Postgres+AGE container at first startup. Change them
# before the first `docker compose up` if you want non-default credentials.
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=governance

# Host-side port mappings. Override only if those ports are already taken
# on your machine (e.g., a separately-installed governance server on 8767).
# GOVERNANCE_HOST_PORT=8767
# LEASE_PLANE_HOST_PORT=8788

# Postgres and Redis are NOT published to the host by default (see
# docker-compose.yml and docs/DEPLOYMENT_SECURITY.md). These two only take
# effect with the opt-in admin overlay:
#   docker compose -f docker-compose.yml -f docker-compose.admin.yml up
# POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5432
# REDIS_HOST_PORT=6379

# The Compose quickstart supplies a loopback-only development default. Override
# it for any shared machine or non-loopback deployment; the lease plane fails
# closed when no bearer is configured outside that Compose wiring. The
# governance plugin's file leases present this bearer too: when you change it,
# put the same line in ~/.config/unitares/secrets.env on the machine where your
# agents run.
# LEASE_PLANE_BEARER_TOKEN=change-me-lease-token

# Identity binding is separate from the shared lease-plane bearer. The Docker
# quickstart enforces short-lived request-bound attestations for maintenance
# leases only. `off` and `log` remain rollout modes; expand the comma-separated
# list only after every producer for a kind carries identity proof.
# UNITARES_LEASE_IDENTITY_BINDING=enforce
# UNITARES_LEASE_IDENTITY_PROOF_FORMAT=attestation  # legacy | hybrid | attestation
# UNITARES_LEASE_IDENTITY_BOUND_SURFACE_KINDS=maintenance

# v1 accepts exactly one issuer -> public-key URL mapping because active lease
# rows do not yet persist issuer-qualified principals. Drain active leases
# before changing that issuer. Remote URLs must use HTTPS; local HTTP requires
# an exact URL exception.
# UNITARES_LEASE_TRUSTED_ISSUERS={"operator-a":"https://a.example/v1/lease-holder/keys"}
# UNITARES_LEASE_TRUST_INSECURE_HTTP_URLS=http://governance-mcp:8767/v1/lease-holder/keys
# SDKs refuse to send continuity credentials over remote HTTP. List only exact
# private-network hostnames that cannot use HTTPS; loopback is always allowed.
# UNITARES_LEASE_INSECURE_GOVERNANCE_HOSTS=governance-mcp

# ===========================================
# DATABASE (Required) - PostgreSQL is the sole backend
# ===========================================
# In docker-compose.yml the DB_POSTGRES_URL is wired automatically from the
# POSTGRES_* values above. Override below only for a non-Docker / external
# Postgres setup (Homebrew install, remote host, etc.).
DB_POSTGRES_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/governance
DB_POSTGRES_MIN_CONN=2
DB_POSTGRES_MAX_CONN=10

# Knowledge graph backend: postgres (default, full-text search), age (opt-in
# graph features; needs the Apache AGE extension in your PostgreSQL), auto
UNITARES_KNOWLEDGE_BACKEND=postgres

# Dialectic session backend: postgres (recommended)
UNITARES_DIALECTIC_BACKEND=postgres

# ===========================================
# SERVER
# ===========================================
# SERVER_HOST=0.0.0.0
# SERVER_PORT=8767

# ===========================================
# MODEL FOR ADVICE AND DIALECTIC REVIEWS (Optional)
# ===========================================
# Name a model to turn on two things: consult (call_model) answers from it, and
# request_review gets a first review from the in-process local reviewer. With
# no reachable model, consult answers "Standard advisory consultation is
# unavailable" (MODEL_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE) and a review records the thesis,
# then waits for a peer or the operator.
#
# The model is reached through one OpenAI-compatible endpoint. Ollama is the
# tested server; others that speak the same routes (vLLM, LM Studio,
# llama.cpp's server) can be named the same way but are not yet verified.
#
# Quickest: `./scripts/unitares model` lists the models your server offers,
# writes these lines and rebuilds the server. By hand, for local Ollama on the
# Docker host (nothing leaves your machine):
#   1. Install Ollama on the host and pull a model: ollama pull gemma4:latest
#   2. Set the two lines below, then rebuild and restart the service (the
#      rebuild installs the model client into an image built before this step):
#        docker compose up -d --build governance-mcp
# UNITARES_MODEL_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1   # base URL, /v1 included
# UNITARES_MODEL_ID=gemma4:latest                                   # a model the server serves
#
# Outside Docker, the default is http://localhost:11434/v1. The older names
# UNITARES_OLLAMA_BASE, UNITARES_OLLAMA_BASE_URL and UNITARES_LLM_MODEL were
# removed in v3.3.0 and are ignored: an install that still sets only those
# gets the defaults. Rename them to UNITARES_MODEL_BASE_URL (a bare Ollama
# root such as http://host.docker.internal:11434 gets /v1 added) and
# UNITARES_MODEL_ID.
#
# privacy='local' requests (the default for consult and call_model, and always
# for the in-process reviewer) go only to an endpoint the server classifies as
# local, from the URL alone, never DNS: loopback and private RFC 1918
# addresses, networks in UNITARES_TRUSTED_NETWORKS, localhost,
# host.docker.internal, and the hostnames listed below. Anything else is
# refused with MODEL_ENDPOINT_NOT_LOCAL. A Compose service such as vllm needs
# the first line; a Tailscale peer needs its range in UNITARES_TRUSTED_NETWORKS
# (below), which on a source install also opens the REST API to that network
# without a token.
# UNITARES_MODEL_LOCAL_HOSTS=vllm,gpu-box.lan
# UNITARES_MODEL_PRIVACY=local   # or external: overrides the classification
#
# Linux: Ollama listens on 127.0.0.1 by default, which the container cannot
# reach. Set OLLAMA_HOST=0.0.0.0 for the Ollama service (or the docker0 bridge
# address) and allow port 11434 from the Docker bridge in your firewall. Ollama
# has no authentication, so do not expose that port beyond this machine.

# ===========================================
# AI SERVICES (Optional - for call_model and semantic search)
# ===========================================
# HF_TOKEN=xxx                         # Hugging Face Inference Providers (call_model cloud fallback)

# HuggingFace embeddings (offline mode recommended)
# HF_HOME=/path/to/.cache/huggingface
# TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=1
# HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1

# ===========================================
# GOVERNANCE TUNING (Optional)
# ===========================================
# UNITARES_PROCESS_UPDATE_RESPONSE_MODE=auto  # auto | minimal | compact | full

# I-channel dynamics mode (default: linear since v5)
# linear:   Prevents boundary saturation, stable equilibrium at I*≈0.80
# logistic: Legacy v4.1 behavior, can saturate I→1.0
# UNITARES_I_DYNAMICS=linear

# ===========================================
# OPERATOR WIRING (Optional; #1791)
# ===========================================
# Required to wire external outcome producers (CI, test runners) through the
# operator-gated /v1/harness/outcome endpoint. Unset = default-deny (403).
# UNITARES_OPERATOR_TOKENS=change-me-operator-token

# Dashboard / telemetry read auth (unset = open on loopback).
# UNITARES_HTTP_API_TOKEN=change-me-api-token

# Networks beyond loopback and the RFC1918 private ranges whose callers skip
# auth in local posture (comma-separated CIDRs; source installs). Nothing
# else is trusted by default. A Tailscale tailnet is 100.64.0.0/10. The same
# list decides which model endpoint addresses count as local. Under Compose,
# callers arrive through the Docker bridge, so there it matters only for the
# model endpoint.
# UNITARES_TRUSTED_NETWORKS=100.64.0.0/10

# Source markers your own substrate runtime writes into outcome evidence
# (comma-separated), trusted beyond the built-in generic ones such as
# sensor_sync. Nothing extra is trusted by default.
# UNITARES_TRUSTED_SUBSTRATE_MARKERS=my_runtime_eisv

# Required before exposing /mcp or REST through a tunnel. A non-empty bearer
# allowlist also makes REST strict by default, disabling trusted-network and
# loopback bypass. Do not set UNITARES_REST_STRICT=0 on a public deployment.
# UNITARES_MCP_BEARER_TOKENS=change-me-hosted-bearer
# Comma-separated Host header values accepted by /mcp. Add the tunnel's public
# hostname without a scheme (for example, governance.example.com).
# UNITARES_MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,governance.example.com
# Comma-separated browser origins accepted by the MCP transport. Include the
# scheme and no trailing slash (for example, https://governance.example.com).
# UNITARES_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:8767,http://127.0.0.1:8767,https://governance.example.com
# Browser MCP clients also cross the outer HTTP CORS middleware. Repeat their
# origins here or the browser preflight fails before reaching /mcp.
# UNITARES_HTTP_CORS_EXTRA_ORIGINS=https://governance.example.com
# WebAuthn relying-party hostname and exact dashboard browser origin. Unset
# means passkey sign-in is off. When the origin is omitted, it defaults to
# https:// plus the RP id.
# UNITARES_DASHBOARD_RP_ID=governance.example.com
# UNITARES_DASHBOARD_ORIGIN=https://governance.example.com
# Opt-in route packs, comma-separated: reference-residents (the reference
# residents' summaries and finding backlog), automation-census
# (/api/automations; host installs only, since it serves a snapshot of the
# host's scheduled jobs and its code is not in the Docker image). Unset mounts
# core routes only. See "Route packs" in docs/operations/resident-roster.md.
# UNITARES_ROUTE_PACKS=reference-residents,automation-census
# A directory of this deployment's own dashboard tabs (dashboard/EXTENSIONS.md).
# Under Compose, also mount it into the governance container at this path.
# UNITARES_DASHBOARD_EXT_DIR=/srv/unitares-dashboard-ext
# A JSON file of the metric names a deployment-specific scraper writes (the
# reference Chronicler's is agents/chronicler/metrics_catalog.json). Unset
# means /v1/metrics lists and accepts only the product metrics. See "Metrics
# extra catalog" in docs/operations/resident-roster.md.
# UNITARES_METRICS_CATALOG_EXTRA=/app/agents/chronicler/metrics_catalog.json
# Singular client credential for in-repo callers such as the lease plane. It
# must exactly match one member of UNITARES_MCP_BEARER_TOKENS.
# UNITARES_MCP_BEARER_TOKEN=change-me-hosted-bearer
# UNITARES_REST_STRICT=1

# Signs short-lived governance identity proofs. Leave unset and the server
# generates one at startup in data/secrets/continuity_token_secret (0600);
# UNITARES_CONTINUITY_TOKEN_SECRET_FILE moves that file. Set this only to share
# a key between processes, and never reuse the HTTP API token for it.
# This secret stays in governance and is never copied into the lease plane.
# UNITARES_CONTINUITY_TOKEN_SECRET=change-me-continuity-secret

# Ed25519 private seed used only by governance to mint request-bound lease
# attestations. Generate 32 random bytes, encode base64url without padding, and
# keep the seed private. Publish/share the issuer and /v1/lease-holder/keys URL,
# never this value. Compose supplies a known local-only development default.
# UNITARES_LEASE_ATTESTATION_SIGNING_KEY=change-me-base64url-ed25519-seed
# UNITARES_LEASE_ATTESTATION_ISSUER=example-operator
# Stable, deployment-specific lease-plane identifier. Governance and the lease
# plane must use the same value; do not reuse it across independent deployments.
# UNITARES_LEASE_ATTESTATION_AUDIENCE=example-operator-production-lease-plane

# Self-reported build sha for /health inside Docker (the image has no .git):
# UNITARES_BUILD_SHA=  # e.g. $(git rev-parse --short HEAD) at compose-up time

# Initial tool advertisement is progressive by default: the core workflow plus
# list_tools, describe_tool and use_tool. Advertise every schema up front with:
# UNITARES_TOOL_ADVERTISEMENT=full
# Legacy GOVERNANCE_TOOL_MODE settings are ignored.
